  "label": "User projected onto the textual material prompting action",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material at the bottom of the meme, which says \"...go ahead...say it!\". This text directly addresses the viewer, inviting them to perform an action (saying 'Allahu Akbar') in a context that equates the phrase with militarized aggression. The imperative 'go ahead...say it!' creates a direct address to the user, making them the subject of the command and thereby projecting them onto this textual element.",
